---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../utils/withBase';
---

<LegalLayout title="Prohibited Items">
  <h1>Prohibited items</h1>
  <p class="legal-updated">As set out in clause 11 of the <a href={withBase("terms")}>Terms and Conditions</a>. Last updated: 1 October 2026.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>General rule</h2>
    <p>Only non-dutiable items may be sent. The following must not be sent or carried through Khepia. If the categories shown in the App differ from this list, <strong>this list prevails</strong>. Khepia decides whether an item is prohibited.</p>
    <p>If your item is not in an allowed App category, email <a href="mailto:khepia.pk@gmail.com">khepia.pk@gmail.com</a> for review before sending. No approval is given for a Prohibited Item.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>You must not send or carry</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Cash and currency of any country</li>
      <li>Gold and jewellery</li>
      <li>Drugs and narcotics</li>
      <li>Medicines of any kind</li>
      <li>Alcohol</li>
      <li>Tobacco and vapes</li>
      <li>Weapons and ammunition</li>
      <li>Explosives and flammable items</li>
      <li>Lithium batteries</li>
      <li>Perishable food</li>
      <li>Live animals and plants</li>
      <li>Counterfeit goods</li>
      <li>Adult material</li>
      <li>High-value electronics</li>
      <li>Mobile phones</li>
      <li>Documents and letters</li>
      <li>Any item on which customs duty or tax is payable in the country of departure or arrival</li>
      <li>Any item whose export, import or carriage is prohibited or restricted under the law of any country of departure, transit or arrival, or under the rules of the airline</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why documents and letters are banned</h2>
    <p>Documents and letters are included because conveying letters is generally reserved to the Federal Government under the Post Office Act, 1898 (subject to limited exceptions).</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>If a prohibited item is involved</h2>
    <p>Sending or carrying a Prohibited Item may be an offence. Khepia may cancel the Booking, suspend the accounts involved, and report the matter to the relevant authorities. Parcel Protection does not apply where a Parcel contained a Prohibited Item or anything not declared.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Passenger duty</h2>
    <p>At handover the Passenger may inspect the items and must refuse the Parcel if they reasonably suspect it contains a Prohibited Item or anything unlawful. Any refusal must be reported at once through the App or to <a href="mailto:khepia.pk@gmail.com">khepia.pk@gmail.com</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Full terms</h2>
    <p>See <a href={withBase("terms#clause-11")}>Terms clause 11</a> and <a href={withBase("customs-and-liability")}>Customs &amp; liability</a> for the complete rules.</p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
